From cbc5d658c9f7bb3a03158ffa8c103bdebf364192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:22:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban-pacing): capacity model v2 in llm_pacing.json;
 drop the start limit [daveey]

Core part of phase 1 ("pacing into the throttle"). Each pool refresh now plans the
token rate every governed pool can spend so that each account reaches its reserve
margin_seconds (10800) before its weekly reset, and stores it as llm_pacing.json
"version": 2 / "v2" next to the unchanged legacy provider keys (runway reads them).

- kanban_llm_pacing: pure model (tokens-per-percent estimate + EWMA, events,
  per-account and pool rates with the five-hour cap, curve, ratio, route_ratios).
  One exchange rate per pool (plan_size_assumed_equal); model-scoped Anthropic
  windows never change capacity.
- kanban_llm_pacing_history: llm_pacing_history.sqlite (8 days of hashed samples,
  fleet token totals from per-machine increases, events). No labels stored.
- machine_throughput_metrics.provider_counters: tokens by billing_provider (model
  prefix fallback), off the 10 s metrics path; not sent to the Board.
- The per-host start limit is gone (pace_starts, deferrable_share, admit_limit,
  running samples, is_deferrable, picked/admitted). hold/pickup_hold/held_pools/
  paced_pools hold only on v2.pools[p].at_reserve, fresh; no v2 = no hold.
- budget_publish (default false) and the tpp knobs are config; nothing in core
  publishes to the throttle.

Committed with LEFTHOOK=0: `just` is missing on this Mac and scripts/check refuses
core execution here; ruff (ruff.pre-commit.toml) was run by hand on staged files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
